      "id": "sec_005",
      "type": "theoretical",
      "title": "EVS Class 1 - Lesson 8: Animal Life > Page-by-Page Content > Page 2",
      "content_text": "- **Text length:** 419 characters - **Word count:** 60 - **Text blocks:** 17 - **Images:** 8 - Image files: - `page_2_img_94.png` (xref: 94) - `page_2_img_96.png` (xref: 96) - `page_2_img_97.png` (xref: 97) - `page_2_img_99.png` (xref: 99) - `page_2_img_101.png` (xref: 101) - `page_2_img_103.png` (xref: 103) - `page_2_img_104.png` (xref: 104) - `page_2_img_45.png` (xref: 45) **Text content:** ``` Animals live both on land and in water. Water animals. Animals that live in water are called “Water Animals or Aquatic Animals”. Land animals. Animals that live on land are called “Land Animals”. Lion Elephant Tiger Birds Birds are the animals with feathers, wings and two-legs and a beak without teeth. Duck Pigeon Parrot 8 Rockland -EVS - Class 1 ``` **Image locations (from text blocks):** - `page_2_img_94.png` - `page_2_img_96.png` - `page_2_img_97.png` - `page_2_img_99.png` - `page_2_img_101.png` - `page_2_img_103.png` - `page_2_img_104.png` - `page_2_img_45.png`",
