    {
      "id": "sec_007",
      "type": "theoretical",
      "title": "EVS Class 1 - Lesson 8: Animal Life > Page-by-Page Content > Page 4",
      "content_text": "- **Text length:** 371 characters - **Word count:** 69 - **Text blocks:** 11 - **Images:** 3 - Image files: - `page_4_img_167.png` (xref: 167) - `page_4_img_169.png` (xref: 169) - `page_4_img_45.png` (xref: 45) **Text content:** ``` Wild Animals : Some animals can be seen only in the forests. They are called “Wild Animals”. Animal Homes : Animals need home to live and food to grow. Different animals eat different kinds of food and live in different homes. Lions : • Lions live in caves in forests. • These caves are called “Dens”. • They eat flesh of other animals. 10 Rockland -EVS - Class 1 ``` **Image locations (from text blocks):** - `page_4_img_167.png` - `page_4_img_169.png` - `page_4_img_45.png`",
