      "id": "sec_008",
      "type": "theoretical",
      "title": "EVS Class 1 - Lesson 8: Animal Life > Page-by-Page Content > Page 5",
      "content_text": "- **Text length:** 462 characters - **Word count:** 84 - **Text blocks:** 16 - **Images:** 10 - Image files: - `page_5_img_183.png` (xref: 183) - `page_5_img_185.png` (xref: 185) - `page_5_img_187.png` (xref: 187) - `page_5_img_189.png` (xref: 189) - `page_5_img_191.png` (xref: 191) - `page_5_img_193.png` (xref: 193) - `page_5_img_195.png` (xref: 195) - `page_5_img_197.png` (xref: 197) - `page_5_img_45.png` (xref: 45) - `page_5_img_47.png` (xref: 47) **Text content:** ``` Rabbits : • They are burrowing animals and live in burrows • They eat vegetables. Birds : • Birds build their own nest. • They eat seeds, berries, fruit, insects, etc. Ants : • They make a hill-like structure using sand called “Anthill”. • Ants live in a group like bees. Domestic and pet animals are kept in human-made homes. A dog lives in a kennel A cow lives in a shed A horse lives in a stable 11 Rockland -EVS - Class 1 ``` **Image locations (from text blocks):** - `page_5_img_183.png` - `page_5_img_185.png` - `page_5_img_187.png` - `page_5_img_189.png` - `page_5_img_191.png` - `page_5_img_193.png` - `page_5_img_195.png` - `page_5_img_197.png` - `page_5_img_45.png` - `page_5_img_47.png`",
