    {
      "id": "sec_009",
      "type": "theoretical",
      "title": "EVS Class 1 - Lesson 8: Animal Life > Page-by-Page Content > Page 6",
      "content_text": "- **Text length:** 882 characters - **Word count:** 135 - **Text blocks:** 21 - **Images:** 4 - Image files: - `page_6_img_222.png` (xref: 222) - `page_6_img_224.png` (xref: 224) - `page_6_img_226.png` (xref: 226) - `page_6_img_45.png` (xref: 45) **Text content:** ``` Assessment • Animals live both on land and in water. • Animals are of different sizes. • Animals that can fly are called birds. • Very small animals are called insects. • Animals that can be kept at home are domestic animals. • Animals that live in jungle are called wild animals. • Different animals live in different homes and eat different foods. Let’s Recall I. Answer the following question. 1. Name any two pet animals. ________________________________________________________________ 2. Where are dogs kept? ________________________________________________________________ • Birds : Animals that can fly are called birds. • Insects : Very small animals are called insects. • Domestic animals: animals that can be kept at home. • Wild animals : Animals that live in jungle.. • Den : Place where lions live. Glossary 12 Rockland -EVS - Class 1 ``` **Image locations (from text blocks):** - `page_6_img_222.png` - `page_6_img_224.png` - `page_6_img_226.png` - `page_6_img_45.png`",
